<title>JAPAN: Japan May domestic vehicle output up 15.8% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May domestic vehicle output up 15.8% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle production rose 15.8 percent in May from a year earlier to 890,611 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It was the third consecutive month in which production was up on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The association said it expected exports in May to have risen about 30 percent from a year earlier. It will announce official export figures on June 26.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of figures in May, with percentage changes:</p>
<p>				   May	yr/yr	pct</p>
<p> Cars			    696,781  up   19.4 percent</p>
<p> Trucks			  188,176  up    3.3 percent</p>
<p> Buses			     5,654  up   48.7 percent</p>
<p>May production by five major manufacturers with percentage changes:</p>
<p>				   May	yr/yr	pct</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     281,050  up    8.2 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor     140,435  up   18.3 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	106,331  up   29.5 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 94,011  up   12.6 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	 75,056  up   35.8 percent</p>
